-- wfl: promoted from tools/spec_r475.json (the R475: the WSG PRECAUTIONS AND PERILS slice with TABLE 39, printed p. 66 - the fifth camping-arc round and the fifth TABLE ROUND of the arc, riding the Table 38 column semantics seam unpinned by R474 (whose boxes covered only the p. 65 grids): the start discipline (2d20 rounds for a character without the fire-building proficiency assuming tools, dry fuel and a breeze of no more than 15 mph; wind over 15 mph or wet fuel means 3d20; no start without tools for the unproficient; no start in wind over 30 mph without magic), the refuel semantics (a fire not refueled in time shrinks to the next lower size; a small fire never goes out within three turns but provides no warmth), the wind resistance semantics (unprotected fires only; falter and flicker with no warmth over the rated velocity; the spread chance to an uncontrollable fire), the capacity semantics (six men at 10 feet from a small fire, doubling per additional 10 feet to 12 men at 20; clustering diminishes by one-third at five feet, one-half at three feet and two-thirds at one foot: 4, 3 and 2 characters), the visibility semantics (yards in moonlight or darkness, one-third off in twilight and one-half off in daylight; the 540-yard large-fire flame; the glow through moderately dense forest; the steep-hill blockage; the smoke reveal), the warmth semantics (the 80-degree minimum safe distance, five segments to move away, three feet from a medium fire and five from a large, the 10-mph calm assumption, windward warmth minus 5 degrees per 10 mph or fraction, leeward safe distance plus 10 feet or one increment whichever is less, and the book own 30-mph medium-fire example: 20 degrees at 20 feet on the windward side instead of 30, 10 feet on the leeward side instead of 3), Table 39 in TWO grids (availability of fuel by terrain and season for a temperate climate: desert 20/20/20/20, forest 70/100/100/100, hills 40/70/70/60, plains 50/70/80/70, swamp 40/30/30/40; and the climate modifiers: desert -20/-10/-10/-20, forest -100/-30/+30/+30, hills -30/-20/+10/+20, mountains -40/-30/+20/+30, plains -60/-40/+20/+20, swamp -40/-20/+10/+20), the every-two-turns further checks, and the start of precautions and perils (no safe fire, the untended conflagration, the cardinal rules, the first rule: no fire on combustibles, 1-3 turns to clear, sparks 100 feet in a strong wind), printed p. 66.);
-- DO NOT hand-edit; the spec JSON stays the adjudicated record.
