th hands and a round from the back or a half from the belt; the cliff face runs 1-2 rounds at 7 hit dice and 1d6, the count from 1d4-1 if warned or 1d6-3 if not, a Climbing Check on any roll of 3 or more and unconsciousness on two 5-or-6 head hits; the base is 10 hit dice and 1d8 with the same head rule and no chance of falling. Mudslides: thick loose topsoil drenched on a moderate or severe slope, half-water mud on the moderate slope and less on the severe; grab rooted vegetation or ride down unhurt unless the valley collects a sinking depth; the swimmer rides on top at 1 inch per round, the non-swimmer treads for half his afloat time then Strength Checks per round and breath and Constitution Checks below. Quicksand: saturated swamp ground, sandy faster than muddy, no suction - tread and swim to safety, the pole rescue for a non-swimmer, and only a swimming-proficient rescuer may enter.",
